{"cross_mech":[],"family":{"alphafold_models":12146,"candidate_reasons":["pfam_previous_unknown_name"],"characterization_status":"","context_evidence_count":null,"cross_mech":{"example_proteins":0,"protein_traits_record":false,"records_by_mech":{},"scanned":false},"curation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","demotion_reasons":[],"description":"This is a family of metal-sensitive repressors, involved in resistance to metal ions. Members of this family bind copper, nickel or cobalt ions via conserved cysteine and histidine residues. In the absence of metal ions, these proteins bind to promoter regions and repress transcription. When bound to metal ions they are unable to bind DNA, leading to transcriptional derepression [[cite:PUB00041403],[cite:PUB00057455],[cite:PUB00057456],[cite:PUB00057457],[cite:PUB00035608]].","domain_architectures":15,"interpro_id":"IPR003735","known_evidence_count":null,"matches":19412,"name":"Metal-sensitive transcriptional repressor","partial_evidence_count":null,"pfam_id":"PF02583","proteins":19403,"proteomes":10791,"short_name":"Trns_repr_metal","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/PF02583","structures":12,"taxa":15418,"unknown_status":"EX_DUF"},"inputs":{"cross_mech":"cross-mech-duf-examples-2026-10-10","members":"pfam-uniprot-uniref90-2026-10-07","protein_examples":"duf-protein-examples-direct-2026-10-13","worklist":"interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10-10"},"members":[],"metadata":{"curation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","history":[{"action":"CREATE","agent":"Codex","curator":"Codex","description":"Primary 2009 anisotropy and 2007 complemented cellular reporter evidence, visually inspected figures, O32222 reference mapping and explicit fit, construct and family-transfer limits; IN_PROGRESS.","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF02583/2026-10-11T060444Z-codex-702c45.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"local_source":"source/history/records/PF02583/2026-10-11T060444Z-codex-702c45.yaml","outcome":"changed","source_path":"history/records/PF02583/2026-10-11T060444Z-codex-702c45.yaml","summary":"Add separate B. subtilis CsoR binding and reporter causal graphs","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:04:44Z","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/DUFMech/blob/0fc1b328560ad751c28eebfb5093414f59205e0c/history/records/PF02583/2026-10-11T060444Z-codex-702c45.yaml"},{"action":"REVIEW","agent":"Codex","curator":"Codex","description":"Two supported edges remain separate: purified Cu-dependent operator-binding decrease and complemented whole-gene reporter derepression. Exact construct, structural steps and additional members remain open; review does not promote IN_PROGRESS or claim independent endorsement.","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF02583/2026-10-11T060649Z-codex-211874.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"local_source":"source/history/records/PF02583/2026-10-11T060649Z-codex-211874.yaml","outcome":"needs_followup","source_path":"history/records/PF02583/2026-10-11T060649Z-codex-211874.yaml","summary":"Retain partial scientific self-review of CsoR causal contexts","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:06:49Z","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/DUFMech/blob/0fc1b328560ad751c28eebfb5093414f59205e0c/history/records/PF02583/2026-10-11T060649Z-codex-211874.yaml"}],"local_source":"source/data/families/PF02583.yaml","record":{"causal_graphs":[{"context":"Figure 7A fluorescence anisotropy uses 4 nM labeled 30-bp operator DNA, 10 mM MES, 0.4 M NaCl, 2 mM DTT, pH 6.5 and 25 C. Protein was expressed in E. coli BL21(DE3) from a Helmann-laboratory pET16b construct. Five readings were averaged at each titration addition.","edges":[{"directness":"DIRECT","edge_id":"copper-decreases-operator-binding","evidence":[{"cache_path":"evidence/PF02583/ma-2009-csor.txt","cache_sha256":"f47da6b66a9d037b0b5f943354248310f220418fa5abadf3b9a642e8ec47d41a","explanation":"Main methods, Table 2 and visually inspected Figure 7A support the qualitative decrease. Unsaturated-fit and second-event limits are retained; E90A in Figure 7B is a coupling control, not proof of an atomic pathway.","reference":"PMID:19249860","snippet":"greatly reduced affinities","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2728441/"},{"cache_path":"evidence/PF02583/O32222-identity.txt","cache_sha256":"05683d8ca8cb0276a8b32108e08f22083b49a044cd5deaa22abe89f6e71cc25d","explanation":"Maps the named B. subtilis protein to the family; not a biochemical experiment or proof of isolated-domain sufficiency.","reference":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/protein/uniprot/O32222/entry/pfam/PF02583/","snippet":"family interval: 17-97, inclusive","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/protein/uniprot/O32222/entry/pfam/PF02583/"}],"evidence_kind":"EXPERIMENTAL","mechanism":"At matched protein concentrations, Cu-loaded CsoR gives lower operator occupancy than apo CsoR in the normalized anisotropy assay, supporting an inhibitory binding response without resolving its structural microsteps.","object":"copza-operator-occupancy","predicate":"decreases","subject":"csor-copper-loaded","support":"OBSERVED"}],"family_mapping":"B. subtilis csoR, formerly yvgZ, is BSU33520 and maps to UniProtKB:O32222, reference sequence version 1, 101 residues, PF02583 at 17-97. The assay uses intact protein, not that isolated interval; exact final tag and construct sequence remain unverified.","graph_id":"bsub-csor-copper-operator-binding","limitations":"The Cu-loaded curve is unsaturated and fitted using the apo maximum anisotropy. The second binding constant is only an upper bound, and individual step constants are not uniquely resolved. E90A loses negative regulation, but no atomic allosteric path is established. Low-micromolar tetramer observations do not exclude nanomolar assembly differences. No family-wide copper specificity, transcription endpoint or cellular efflux is inferred.","nodes":[{"grounding":["UniProtKB:O32222"],"label":"Cu(I) loading of purified B. subtilis CsoR","node_id":"csor-copper-loaded","node_type":"PERTURBATION"},{"label":"CsoR occupancy of the synthetic copZA operator","node_id":"copza-operator-occupancy","node_type":"STATE"}],"scope":"Intact purified B. subtilis CsoR compared in apo and Cu(I)-loaded states on a synthetic copZA operator; not cellular transcription or an isolated PF02583 domain.","scope_status":"MECHANISTIC","taxon":"NCBITaxon:224308","title":"Copper loading reduces purified B. subtilis CsoR operator binding"},{"context":"HB7352 csoR::spc is compared with HB7358 reporter control and HB7356 csoR::spc amyE::csoR-cat complementation. Overnight cultures were diluted 1:100 into LB and grown to mid-exponential phase at 37 C and 225 rpm. The adopted edge is the no-added-CuSO4 comparison; the figure also includes 0.5 mM CuSO4. Figure 2A states three experiments with total N=7.","edges":[{"directness":"INDIRECT","edge_id":"csor-null-increases-reporter","evidence":[{"cache_path":"evidence/PF02583/smaldone-2007-csor.txt","cache_sha256":"8d30323834ea6f760de6cc04922ad259c7f9869e15a04803f85d8dbb11cc385b","explanation":"Table 1, reporter methods and visually inspected Figure 2A support the null-versus-control effect and complementation. The endpoint remains reporter enzyme activity, separate from the 2009 binding assay.","reference":"PMID:18048925","snippet":"the copZA promoter was expressed constitutively","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3019219/"},{"cache_path":"evidence/PF02583/O32222-identity.txt","cache_sha256":"05683d8ca8cb0276a8b32108e08f22083b49a044cd5deaa22abe89f6e71cc25d","explanation":"Reference locus and family mapping only, not evidence for the reporter's causal response.","reference":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/protein/uniprot/O32222/entry/pfam/PF02583/","snippet":"gene: csoR; synonym: yvgZ; ordered locus: BSU33520","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/protein/uniprot/O32222/entry/pfam/PF02583/"}],"evidence_kind":"EXPERIMENTAL","mechanism":"The csoR null strain has elevated reporter activity without added copper; an ectopic csoR copy restores regulation, supporting a gene-dependent derepression phenotype.","object":"copza-lacz-output","predicate":"increases","subject":"csor-null","support":"OBSERVED"}],"family_mapping":"CU1065 is a W168 attSPbeta trpC2 derivative. Its yvgZ/csoR locus corresponds to reference O32222, BSU33520, sequence version 1, PF02583 at 17-97 of 101 residues. Whole-gene replacement does not establish an isolated-domain effect.","graph_id":"bsub-csor-null-copza-reporter","limitations":"Beta-galactosidase activity is reporter output, not a direct measurement of native copZA RNA, polymerase occupancy or copper efflux. Ectopic complementation supports gene dependence without resolving each intervening step. The paper corrects an earlier YhdQ/CueR assignment caused by a wrong reporter in the old strain; that claim is not combined with this graph. Other family members and growth endpoints remain separate.","nodes":[{"grounding":["UniProtKB:O32222"],"label":"Whole-gene csoR null allele in the CU1065 reporter strain","node_id":"csor-null","node_type":"PERTURBATION"},{"label":"PcopZA-cat-lacZ beta-galactosidase output without added copper","node_id":"copza-lacz-output","node_type":"PHENOTYPE"}],"scope":"Whole-gene csoR replacement in B. subtilis CU1065 derivatives carrying SPbeta(PcopZA-cat-lacZ); a cellular reporter phenotype, not direct polymerase exclusion.","scope_status":"PHENOTYPIC","taxon":"NCBITaxon:224308","title":"Loss of csoR increases copZA reporter output without added copper"}],"characterization_status":"UNSCORED","counters":{"alphafold_models":12146,"domain_architectures":15,"matches":19412,"proteins":19403,"proteomes":10791,"structures":12,"taxa":15418},"curation_events":[{"action":"CREATE","curator":"Codex","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF02583/2026-10-11T060444Z-codex-702c45.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"outcome":"changed","summary":"Add separate B. subtilis CsoR binding and reporter causal graphs","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:04:44Z"},{"action":"REVIE